{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s plugin system is a single protocol ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") with four lifecycle hooks and an ordered registry ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). All store extensibility flows through this contract. The built-in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" use it, and so do domain-specific features like killswitch enforcement and paywall management."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The Dispatch Lifecycle","anchor":"The-Dispatch-Lifecycle","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every call to "},{"code":"store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" drives plugins through a four-phase lifecycle:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["plugins.willReduce(state:action:)      \/\/ 1. Pre-reduce (read-only state)","appReducer.reduce(state:action:...)    \/\/ 2. App reducer runs","pluginEffects = plugins.reduce(...)    \/\/ 3. Plugin reducers run","plugins.afterReduce(state:action:)     \/\/ 4. Post-reduce cleanup"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generic "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" implements this lifecycle internally. You don’t write "},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand — "},{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles packing, reducing, plugin hooks, unpacking, and effect dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fifth method, "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", runs once at shutdown to drain async buffers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All four hooks have default no-op implementations. Each plugin overrides only what it needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Core Middleware vs Domain Plugins","anchor":"Core-Middleware-vs-Domain-Plugins","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin system serves two structurally different roles. Recognizing which one a plugin fills determines where it lives, which hooks it uses, and how it couples to the host app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Core Middleware","anchor":"Core-Middleware","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" are "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"action-agnostic infrastructure","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". They never inspect the "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type, never dispatch actions, and never return effects. They couple only to the shape of state:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" needs keypaths to ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"text":" properties.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" needs ","type":"text"},{"code":"State: Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so it can snapshot and compare.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because they don’t touch actions, they work with any app that uses Swidux — no wiring required beyond construction."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Domain Plugins","anchor":"Domain-Plugins","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Killswitch, parental gate, and paywall plugins are "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"domain-specific modules","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" that ship as separate library targets ("},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). They own their own state slices and action enums, dispatch effects, and must be explicitly wired into the host app’s root types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each domain plugin stores three wiring pieces:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["private let stateKeyPath: WritableKeyPath<RootState, FeatureState>","private let toRootAction: @Sendable (FeatureAction) -> RootAction","private let extractAction: @Sendable (RootAction) -> FeatureAction?"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The host app provides these at init — the plugin never assumes a specific root type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Comparison","anchor":"Comparison","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core Middleware"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain Plugins"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Action knowledge","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full — extracts and lifts actions"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lifecycle hooks","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Returns effects","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State coupling","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" constraint"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath to plugin’s own state slice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wiring","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construction only"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keypath + action lifter + action extractor"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Target","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Separate library target"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Opt-in","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Instantiate and register"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add state, action case, and register"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"text":"The Decision Rule","anchor":"The-Decision-Rule","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does the middleware need to know your action type? If "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s core middleware — put it in "},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"yes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s a domain plugin — give it its own target and use "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important","style":"important","type":"aside"},{"text":"Hook Selection Guide","anchor":"Hook-Selection-Guide","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"willReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Capture state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the reducer mutates it. State is read-only. Use for snapshots (undo) or pre-mutation analytics.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"reduce(state:action:) -> Effect?","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Handle domain-specific actions ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the app reducer. Mutate the plugin’s state slice and return effects. This is the only hook that can dispatch actions or do async work.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce(state:action:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Observe state ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" all reducing is done. Use for persistence draining, logging, or metrics. Cannot return effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"flush() async","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Shutdown hook. Flush pending async buffers (persistence writes, analytics batches). Called once when the app exits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Registration Order","anchor":"Registration-Order","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","type":"reference"},{"text":" executes plugins in registration order. Recommended ordering:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. Must snapshot before any mutation","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. Drains changelogs after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. Domain plugins in any order","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Undo must come first — it snapshots state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", before the app reducer or any plugin modifies it. Persistence typically comes next so its ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drain sees the final state. Domain plugins use only ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so their relative order rarely matters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Service-Result Actions and Transition Observation","anchor":"Service-Result-Actions-and-Transition-Observation","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"service-result action"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"verdictReceived","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshSucceeded","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — fires on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" fetch, refresh, or stream tick, not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when the value changed, and unconditionally writes its payload to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state slice. The payload is frequently identical to what is already there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(a re-delivered entitlement, an unchanged remote config).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Do ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" map analytics or side effects to the raw service-result action:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it fires duplicates by design. Observe the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state slice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — or a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derived from it — instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State observation is already deduplicated by the framework. ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"packs the observer into a value-type snapshot, lets reducers mutate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"snapshot, then writes back via ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For a leaf slice that write","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a plain assignment whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setter equality-gates ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values, so a slice whose value did not change emits no notification — and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value-diffing consumer such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsIdentity.userProperties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" re-evaluates and diffs every non-analytics dispatch) sees exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"real transitions. This dedup is a property of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-plugin guard, so a no-op service-result cycle is silent to state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observers without any extra reducer logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Next Steps","anchor":"Next-Steps","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},{"text":" — Step-by-step guide to creating a domain plugin","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"text":" — Configure the built-in persistence middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},{"text":" — Add undo\/redo with the built-in undo middleware","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true,"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","title":"UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","title":"Design Principles"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","title":"PluginHost","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","title":"Store","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Store"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","title":"EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","title":"Persistence Middleware","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","title":"Architecture & Performance","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","title":"Undo \/ Redo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}}}